==English==

===Etymology===
First attested from 1350 to 1470,<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=4}}</ref> from {{inh|en|enm|abetement}}, from {{der|en|xno|-}}, from {{der|en|fro|abeter}} + {{m|en|-ment}}. See {{m|en|abet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈbɛt.mənt/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-abetment.oga|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-ca-abetment.ogg|a=CA}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|law}} The act of [[abet|abetting]] or assisting in a [[crime]], [[wrongdoing]] etc. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
# [[encouragement|Encouragement]] or assistance. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}

